        <mxCell id="t30" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color:#2f5597&quot;&gt;&amp;#9644;&amp;#9644;&lt;/span&gt; Cat6 / physical link &amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#b85450&quot;&gt;- - -&lt;/span&gt; management (telnet / SSH) &amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#9673a6&quot;&gt;&amp;#9644;&amp;#9644;&lt;/span&gt; A/V control (adb, HDMI, CEC)&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#bf9000&quot;&gt;- - -&lt;/span&gt; cloud egress &amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#999&quot;&gt;- - -&lt;/span&gt; Wi-Fi / DHCP&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Invariants worth keeping in mind&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; One L3 subnet, zero routed hops &amp;#8212; latency differences are L2 switch hops only.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; All hub logic is &lt;b&gt;ucode (.uc)&lt;/b&gt;; /bin/sh only wraps ping / adb / nc.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; CGI never touches a device synchronously &amp;#8212; pollers own all device I/O, CGI reads /tmp.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Huawei APs accept exactly &lt;b&gt;one&lt;/b&gt; telnet session; the poller holds it most of the time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Mi TV adb is single-authorised: drive it from the router only." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="610" x="1310" y="1066" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
